# env.required — without this the monitor cannot function.
# An answer-engine key (Perplexity canonical) — query_engines.py needs at least one of the
# engine keys or it exits non-zero. Querying answer engines IS the task here (inherent), so
# one engine key stays required; the ADDITIONAL engines are env.optional and the run degrades
# to whatever keys are present. If you standardize on a different single engine, set that
# engine's key instead (OPENAI_API_KEY / GEMINI_API_KEY / TAVILY_API_KEY).
PERPLEXITY_API_KEY
